  VALUES
    ('ios_crash_gate', 'iOS crash gate', 'blocked', 'Authenticated App Store Connect reports two crashes for public iOS 1.0.1 (4): one on 2026-08-25 and one on 2026-08-29. The 2026-08-29 event maps to iPhone; the 2026-08-25 device/OS dimension is suppressed or unavailable. Neither event exposes a diagnostic, stack, incident/signature ID, or crashed-binary UUID. Historical product commit 2cdd4387fc2b8b0f4cd3e3a873f019a6ca8a3652 passed shared Simulator and Apple surface-state tests, and its independently byte-verified distribution-signed 1.1.0 (6) IPA completed Transporter delivery and became VALID and APP_STORE_ELIGIBLE. It is not the crashed public build, has not been installed through TestFlight, and cannot identify either production event. Replacement source ba824beae5e72653e42af2b8b78286f61415e3ab advances Apple to build 7 but has no signed candidate yet. Diagnostic access and symbolication, protected build-7 signing, TestFlight distribution, an exact physical iPhone/iPad/widget/watch pass, and post-rollout crash evidence remain missing.', 'Obtain and symbolicate any diagnostic Apple exposes, sign and independently verify build 7, complete the iPhone/iPad/widget/watch matrix, and collect post-rollout evidence'),
    ('open_meteo_promotion_clearance', 'Open-Meteo promotion clearance', 'pass', 'The complete authenticated Gmail record was checked read-only on 2026-08-29. The 06:05:07 +05:00 request described Nimbo as free and non-monetized, with no subscriptions, advertising, paid features, affiliate links, accounts, analytics SDK, or sale of user data, and limited promotion to unpaid localized posts, one personalized contact plus at most one follow-up, genuine Apple/Google editorial submissions, and ordinary unpaid links. At 17:25 +05:00, Nicoletta Addimando via OpenMeteo GmbH replied in ticket 234272 and explicitly confirmed that under those terms Nimbo is entitled to use the non-commercial API. This pass is limited to that exact scope and the published Free API limits; monetization, paid promotion, attribution removal, limit changes, or other material facts require a new licensing decision.', 'Preserve the confirmed scope and reopen licensing review before any material monetization, promotion, attribution, endpoint, or usage-limit change'),
    ('release_artifact_source_sync', 'Release artifact source sync', 'blocked', 'Product/build-input commit ba824beae5e72653e42af2b8b78286f61415e3ab resolves to Android phone 1.1.0 (9), Wear OS 1.1.0 (1000009), and Apple 1.1.0 (7). The phone legacy-icon source defect is fixed and the API-24 debug launcher check passes, but no protected signed candidate or independent byte verification is bound to this revision. The former phone vc8, Wear vc1000008, and Apple build 6 candidates remain immutable historical evidence tied to revision 2cdd4387fc2b8b0f4cd3e3a873f019a6ca8a3652; their Internal-track, Transporter, and physical results do not transfer. Hosted exact-source CI, protected signing, full-byte verification, Internal/TestFlight delivery, and applicable physical QA are required before any production promotion. The gate remains blocked.', 'Pass exact-source hosted CI, protected signing, independent full-byte verification, and Internal/TestFlight delivery for the replacement set'),
    ('android_physical_smoke', 'Android device smoke', 'blocked', 'Historical product commit 2cdd4387fc2b8b0f4cd3e3a873f019a6ca8a3652 retains the independently byte-verified phone vc8 and Wear vc1000008 candidates and the Play-delivered API-25 functional, accessibility, background, widget, offline, and recovery evidence. That exact phone package nevertheless displayed the Android Studio template launcher icon and remains ineligible for production. Replacement source ba824beae5e72653e42af2b8b78286f61415e3ab advances the phone to 1.1.0 (9), removes all ten template WebPs, deterministically generates branded square and round legacy resources from the canonical Nimbo icon, assembles successfully, and renders the Nimbo mark in Launcher3 on an API-24 emulator. No upload-signed or Play-delivered vc9 exists yet, so the emulator result is implementation evidence only. Exact protected signing, independent byte verification, Internal delivery, physical API-24/25 launcher smoke, physical tablet and paired Wear coverage, and post-delivery vitals remain missing. The Samsung API-36 device contains user data and was not modified. Production was not changed. The gate remains blocked.', 'Sign and independently verify vc9, deliver it through Play Internal, then repeat physical API-24/25 launcher and remaining tablet/Wear QA'),
    ('ios_physical_smoke', 'iOS physical smoke', 'blocked', 'Historical product commit 2cdd4387fc2b8b0f4cd3e3a873f019a6ca8a3652 retains independently byte-verified distribution-signed Apple 1.1.0 (6). That exact IPA completed Transporter delivery and App Store Connect reported it VALID and APP_STORE_ELIGIBLE, but no TestFlight physical install or production availability was proved. Replacement coordinated source ba824beae5e72653e42af2b8b78286f61415e3ab advances Apple to build 7; no signed build 7 exists yet, so build 6 evidence does not transfer. The iPhone 14 Pro remains unavailable; the paired iPad mini 5 app inventory is blocked by CoreDevice/mobile-image-mounter state, and the paired Series 5 watch has Developer Mode disabled. Protected signing, independent byte verification, TestFlight distribution/install, the physical iPhone/iPad/widget/watch matrix, crash diagnosis, and post-rollout crash evidence remain missing. The gate remains blocked.', 'Sign and independently verify build 7, distribute it through TestFlight, then install and run the complete iPhone/iPad/widget/watch matrix'),
    ('domain_activation', 'Domain activation', 'pass', 'At 2026-08-29 10:40–10:41 +05:00, authenticated GitHub Pages settings showed DNS check successful and Enforce HTTPS enabled. The Let''s Encrypt certificate has CN nimbo.uz, SANs nimbo.uz/www.nimbo.uz, and validates for both hosts. WHOIS, .uz delegation, authoritative Cloudflare records, and independent 1.1.1.1/8.8.8.8 resolution pass. HTTPS returns 200 with verification result 0 for all 12 published UZ-root/RU/EN landing, press, privacy, and support routes plus growth, robots, sitemap, and the valid metadata schema. HTTP apex redirects to HTTPS; HTTP www reaches HTTPS apex in two redirects; HTTPS www redirects directly to HTTPS apex. All 12 localized HTML routes have the expected HTTPS canonical and language. Uzbek intentionally uses ' || chr(47) || ' rather than a separate ' || chr(47) || 'uz' || chr(47) || ' route.', 'Maintain dated DNS, certificate, redirect, canonical, and localized-route verification at each release'),
    ('store_policy_console_clearance', 'Store policy console clearance', 'pass', 'The 2026-08-28 App Store read-only check found no open review/compliance action. Google Play reported no policy issues at 2026-08-29 13:12 +05:00; production remained active at 1.0.2 (6), 100%. Authenticated read-only checks through 2026-09-01 05:05 Asia/Tashkent confirm that review request 14 contains only the Uzbekistan Custom Store Listing en-US and ru-RU store data and remains На рассмотрении. Managed publishing is off and the latest verified publication remains 2026-08-27. A fresh logged-out gl=UZ&hl=uz page still renders the old public title Nimbo, so approval and propagation are not claimed. This proves review submission, not approval, publication, propagation, or a later policy guarantee. See growth/quality/store-policy-console-2026-08-28.md, growth/quality/google-play-console-2026-08-29.md, growth/quality/google-play-console-2026-08-31.md, and growth/quality/store-release-recheck-2026-09-01.md.', 'Re-check both app-global store policy surfaces at the next evidence cutoff')
